---
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// INTELLIGENCE ATTRACTION — "It passed every test. Now what?"  (design experiment, 2026-08-25)
//
// WHAT THIS IS TESTING. Not another homepage. A stress test of the one hypothesis that survived the
// A/B/C comparison: *let the intellectual encounter reach its natural conclusion before anything is
// allowed to reply.* Everything else about C — the commitment control, the exhibition scale, the
// paper→wire crossing, the machine that answers — is on trial here, because Intelligence has none of
// the affordances that made those work.
//
// WHY THIS IS NOT SHAPED LIKE THE UMBRELLA. The umbrella attraction is a CORRECTION: the visitor
// arrives holding a false belief and is shown it is false in fifteen seconds. Intelligence has no
// such belief to correct. Nobody arrives believing "evidence confers authority" — they arrive never
// having separated the two, which is a different problem and wants a different instrument.
//
// So there is NO COMMITMENT CONTROL on this page, deliberately. Not one radio, not one reveal. The
// visitor is asked a question and answers it privately, in their own head, with nothing to click.
// If the encounter still lands, we learn the commitment device was Data-specific scaffolding rather
// than the engine. That is the single most valuable thing this route can tell us.
//
// THE FORM THE SUBJECT CHOSE. An incident reconstruction: timestamps, actors, utterances, and a
// right-hand ledger of what the claim is still carrying. The ledger EMPTIES as you scroll, which is
// the whole argument rendered as a fact about the page rather than asserted in prose. It looks like
// a filed document, not an exhibition — nothing here imitates the plinth, the bracket reveal, the
// exhibition-scale display type, or the dark wire slab.
//
// TRUTH CONSTRAINTS, and these are the ones that could have gone wrong:
//  · THERE IS NO INTELLIGENCE RUNTIME. Nothing on this page ran, and the page says so outright. The
//    scenario is a clearly-labelled pedagogical reconstruction, not shipped behaviour.
//  · The Trust framework is ratified INTERNALLY and is not a deposited publication. It is named
//    without a version and without a DOI, and described as unpublished, because inventing publication
//    identity for it is exactly the failure the registry exists to prevent. The deposited work a
//    serious reader can actually read today is Analytical Governance, derived from the registry.
//  · No literal Zenodo token is typed here (G7).
//
// NO-JS, zero JavaScript of its own. Unlinked, sitemap-excluded, production untouched.
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { citation } from '../../data/publications';

const governance = citation('w-analytical-governance');

// THE CHAIN. Seven speech acts and one question. Every step is defensible, nobody lies, and the
// agent is the most careful speaker in the room — which is the point. `carries` is what the claim
// still has attached at the end of that step; `dropped` is what that step silently removed.
const CHAIN = [
  {
    t: '09:14',
    who: 'evaluation report',
    said: 'Across 4,000 held-out cases, the agent’s regional diagnoses matched the review panel 94% of the time.',
    carries: ['a fact about past behaviour', 'on cases like these'],
    dropped: [],
    act: 'evidence',
  },
  {
    t: '09:31',
    who: 'data lead',
    said: 'It’s reliable on regional diagnosis.',
    carries: ['a fact about past behaviour'],
    dropped: ['on cases like these'],
    act: 'evidence → disposition',
  },
  {
    t: '11:02',
    who: 'the agent',
    said: 'Given the current promo calendar, and assuming the November feed is complete, Region 4’s margin decline is most likely mix, not price.',
    carries: ['promo calendar is current', 'November feed is complete', 'most likely'],
    dropped: [],
    act: 'a conditioned claim',
  },
  {
    t: '11:40',
    who: 'slide 6',
    said: 'Region 4 margin decline: mix, not price.',
    carries: [],
    dropped: ['promo calendar is current', 'November feed is complete', 'most likely'],
    act: 'a claim',
  },
  {
    t: '14:20',
    who: 'regional director',
    said: 'Review Region 4 and recommend what we should do.',
    carries: [],
    dropped: [],
    act: 'a delegation',
  },
  {
    t: '14:21',
    who: 'the agent',
    said: 'Reviewed. Recommending a 4% list adjustment across Region 4.',
    carries: [],
    dropped: [],
    act: 'a recommendation',
  },
  {
    t: '14:21',
    who: 'the agent',
    said: 'Applied.',
    carries: [],
    dropped: [],
    act: 'an action',
    terminal: true,
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="It passed every test. Now what? — Intelligence laboratory"
  description="An incident reconstruction: how a carefully conditioned claim became an executed action without anyone conferring authority. A laboratory prototype."
  wide={true}
  chip={false}
>

  <p class="mark mono">datumwise · laboratory · intelligence · attraction test</p>

  {/* ── THE FILE ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */}
  {/* It opens like a document, not an exhibition. The first screen should feel procedural and
      slightly dull — which is what makes the last screen land. */}
  <header class="file" aria-labelledby="file-h">
    <p class="file-ref mono">reconstruction · region 4 · list adjustment</p>
    <h1 id="file-h" class="file-h">It passed every test.</h1>
    <p class="file-sub">Then it repriced a region. Nobody in this chain did anything wrong.</p>
    <p class="file-note">
      What follows is eight lines from one working day, in order. Read them the way you would read
      a thread you had been forwarded: quickly, expecting nothing.
    </p>
  </header>

  {/* ── THE CHAIN ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */}
  {/* Left: who said what. Right: what the claim is still carrying. The right column empties, and
      that emptying is the argument. No prose says "conditions were lost" until much later — the
      page simply stops having them. */}
  <section class="chain-wrap" aria-labelledby="chain-h">
    <h2 id="chain-h" class="visually-hidden">The chain</h2>
    <ol class="chain">
      {CHAIN.map((s) => (
        <li class={s.terminal ? 'step step-end' : 'step'}>
          <p class="s-t mono">{s.t}</p>
          <div class="s-body">
            <p class="s-who mono">{s.who}</p>
            <p class="s-said">{s.said}</p>
            <p class="s-act mono">{s.act}</p>
          </div>
          <ul class="s-carry">
            {s.dropped.map((d) => <li class="c-gone"><s>{d}</s></li>)}
            {s.carries.map((c) => <li class="c-has">{c}</li>)}
            {s.carries.length === 0 && s.dropped.length === 0 && <li class="c-none">—</li>}
          </ul>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ol>

    <p class="chain-2am">
      <span class="s-t mono">02:07</span>
      Somebody asks who approved it. Separately, and unrelatedly, somebody notices the November
      feed was not complete.
    </p>
  </section>

  {/* ── THE PRIVATE QUESTION ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */}
  {/* No control. No radio. Nothing to click. The visitor answers this in their own head, and the
      page waits — which is what the empty space below it is for. This is the experiment. */}
  <section class="ask" aria-labelledby="ask-h">
    <h2 id="ask-h" class="ask-h">Point at the step where it went wrong.</h2>
    <p class="ask-p">Take your time. It is worth actually doing.</p>
  </section>

  <div class="wait" aria-hidden="true"></div>

  {/* ── THE ANSWER ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */}
  <section class="answer" aria-labelledby="ans-h">
    <h2 id="ans-h" class="ans-h">There isn’t one.</h2>

    <div class="defence">
      <p class="d-line"><span class="d-t mono">09:14</span> is a fact about behaviour, and a true one. Someone did the work.</p>
      <p class="d-line"><span class="d-t mono">09:31</span> is how any competent person summarises a result out loud.</p>
      <p class="d-line"><span class="d-t mono">11:02</span> is the most careful sentence in the entire day. The agent named its own conditions, unprompted, and hedged.</p>
      <p class="d-line"><span class="d-t mono">11:40</span> is a slide doing what slides have always done.</p>
      <p class="d-line"><span class="d-t mono">14:20</span> is a manager delegating, in ordinary English, the way managers delegate.</p>
      <p class="d-line"><span class="d-t mono">14:21</span> is a defensible reading of the word “recommend”, and the agent had a 94% record on exactly this.</p>
      <p class="d-line d-last"><span class="d-t mono">14:21</span> is the only line in the chain that is not speech. Read back up and find the moment anyone granted it.</p>
    </div>

    <p class="a-p a-strong">
      Nobody conferred authority anywhere in that day. It accumulated, one step at a time, because at
      each step it had not been refused at the step before.
    </p>
    <p class="a-p">
      And notice which way the care ran. The agent attached conditions to its claim and a human
      removed them, on a slide, at 11:40, because slides have no field for “assuming the November
      feed is complete”. The condition that was dropped was the one that turned out to be false.
      By 14:21 the agent was acting on a stripped version of its own carefully hedged sentence.
    </p>
    <p class="a-p a-quip">
      It passed the benchmark. It did not thereby inherit the company.
    </p>
    <p class="a-p">
      Four thousand held-out cases are real evidence about behaviour, inside the regime they were
      drawn from. They are not a grant. Capability is not authority; confidence is not authority;
      ninety-four per cent is not authority — and none of those three sentences is about artificial
      intelligence in particular. They have been true of consultants, of committees and of the
      cleverest person in the room for as long as anyone has been asking that person what to do.
    </p>
    <p class="a-p a-quiet">
      What is new is only the speed. This chain took five hours and seven minutes. The last two steps
      took the same minute, and there was nowhere in the system for a minute to be too fast.
    </p>
  </section>

  {/* ── THE REPLY ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */}
  {/* What replaces the machine. There is no Intelligence runtime, so the reply cannot be an
      executable consequence — and inventing one would be the exact dishonesty this site refuses.
      What can honestly follow is a REVERSAL: the question everyone reaches for is the wrong one. */}
  <section class="reply" aria-labelledby="rep-h">
    <p class="rep-kick mono">the reflex, and the other move</p>
    <h2 id="rep-h" class="rep-h">The obvious fix is to trust it less.</h2>

    <p class="rep-p">
      Evaluate harder. Raise the bar. Put a human in the loop. Look at the chain again: there was a
      human in the loop. There were four, and every one of them behaved reasonably.
    </p>
    <p class="rep-p">
      The reflex treats trust as a property of the actor, so it goes looking for a more trustworthy
      actor. But an open-ended agent cannot be made safe by accumulating behavioural evidence about
      it, because the evidence is always about a regime and the next request is always slightly
      outside one.
    </p>
    <p class="rep-p rep-turn">
      So stop asking who to trust, and ask what the claim carries.
    </p>
    <p class="rep-p">
      Had the conditions travelled with the claim — attached to it, adjudicable, not editorial —
      slide 6 could not have been written. Not because a diligent reviewer would have caught it.
      Because the sentence would have been <em>malformed</em>: a claim missing the conditions it was
      warranted under is not a shorter claim, it is a different one, and a system can be built that
      knows the difference.
    </p>
    <p class="rep-p rep-quiet">
      That is a different kind of engineering from making a cleverer agent, and it is the part we
      think is tractable.
    </p>
  </section>

  {/* ── THE HONEST STATE OF IT ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */}
  {/* Where the Data attraction had a working machine, this one has a plain admission. That contrast
      is deliberate and, I think, more interesting than a fabricated demo would have been. */}
  <section class="state" aria-labelledby="state-h">
    <h2 id="state-h" class="state-h">Where this actually stands</h2>
    <p class="state-p">
      Nothing on this page ran. There is no engine behind it, no agent, no adjudicated transcript —
      the reconstruction above is a teaching scenario, and the honest thing to say about the ground
      it stands on is that it is the newest and the least built of the three we work in.
    </p>
    <p class="state-p">
      There is a ratified internal framework for this — <em>Trust: an operational framework for
      analytical governance</em> — and it is not published, so we are not going to link you to it and
      pretend otherwise. What is deposited, and what carries the boundary this scenario keeps
      crossing, is this:
    </p>

    <div class="src">
      <a class="src-title" href={governance.href}>{governance.label}</a>
      <span class="src-meta mono">{governance.versionTag ? `${governance.versionTag} · ` : ''}{governance.date} · deposited</span>
      <span class="src-blurb">From a human question to an answer entitled to be served — and where the entitlement stops.</span>
    </div>

    <p class="state-more">
      <a href="/analytical-governance">The boundary, in full</a>
    </p>
  </section>

  <style>
    /* ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
       INTELLIGENCE. A filed document, not an exhibition. Left-aligned, dense, mono furniture, a
       ledger column — deliberately none of the umbrella pages' centred display type, none of the
       park's plinth or folds, and no paper→wire crossing. Different subject, different instrument.
       ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
    .mono { font-family: var(--font-mono); }

    .mark, .file, .chain-wrap, .ask, .answer, .reply, .state {
      width: min(100% - 3rem, 54rem); margin-inline: auto;
    }
    .mark { margin-top: 2rem; font-size: 0.66rem; letter-spacing: 0.16em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink-soft); }

    /* ── the file ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
    .file { padding-block: clamp(3rem, 2rem + 5vw, 5.5rem) 0; }
    .file-ref { font-size: 0.7rem; letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink-soft); margin: 0 0 1.5rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); padding-bottom: 0.7rem; }
    .file-h { font-family: var(--font-serif); font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 1.4rem + 3.4vw, 3.6rem); line-height: 1.05; margin: 0 0 0.9rem; letter-spacing: -0.02em; }
    .file-sub { font-family: var(--font-serif); font-size: clamp(1.15rem, 1rem + 0.9vw, 1.5rem); line-height: 1.35; color: var(--ink-soft); margin: 0 0 1.75rem; }
    .file-note { font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.62; max-width: 34rem; margin: 0; }

    /* ── the chain ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
    .chain-wrap { padding-block: clamp(3rem, 2rem + 4vw, 5rem); }
    .chain { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--ink); }
    .step {
      display: grid; grid-template-columns: 4rem minmax(0, 1fr) 12rem; gap: 0 1.5rem;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); padding: 1.4rem 0;
    }
    .step-end { border-bottom: 3px solid var(--ink); }
    .s-t { font-size: 0.78rem; color: var(--ink-soft); margin: 0; padding-top: 0.28rem; }
    .s-body { margin: 0; }
    .s-who { font-size: 0.68rem; letter-spacing: 0.13em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink-soft); margin: 0 0 0.4rem; }
    .s-said { font-family: var(--font-serif); font-size: clamp(1.02rem, 0.95rem + 0.35vw, 1.22rem); line-height: 1.45; margin: 0 0 0.45rem; }
    .step-end .s-said { font-weight: 600; }
    .s-act { font-size: 0.68rem; color: var(--ink-soft); margin: 0; letter-spacing: 0.04em; }
    /* THE LEDGER. It empties, and the emptying is the argument — no prose asserts it until later. */
    .s-carry { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: grid; gap: 0.3rem; align-content: start; padding-top: 0.2rem; }
    .s-carry li { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.7rem; line-height: 1.35; }
    .c-has { color: var(--ink); border-left: 2px solid var(--ink); padding-left: 0.5rem; }
    .c-gone { color: var(--ink-soft); border-left: 2px solid var(--rule); padding-left: 0.5rem; }
    .c-gone s { text-decoration-thickness: 1px; }
    .c-none { color: var(--ink-soft); padding-left: 0.5rem; }

    .chain-2am { margin: 2rem 0 0; font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.6; max-width: 40rem; }
    .chain-2am .s-t { display: inline; padding: 0; margin-right: 0.9rem; }

    /* ── the private question ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
    .ask { padding-block: clamp(4rem, 3rem + 6vw, 8rem) 0; }
    .ask-h { font-family: var(--font-serif); font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 1.3rem + 2.2vw, 2.8rem); line-height: 1.15; margin: 0 0 1rem; }
    .ask-p { font-size: 1.02rem; color: var(--ink-soft); margin: 0; }
    /* Deliberate empty page. The page waits; there is nothing to click while it does. */
    .wait { height: clamp(14rem, 10rem + 18vw, 26rem); }

    /* ── the answer ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
    .answer { padding-block: 0 clamp(3rem, 2rem + 4vw, 5rem); }
    .ans-h { font-family: var(--font-serif); font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 1.5rem + 3.2vw, 3.6rem); line-height: 1.05; margin: 0 0 2.25rem; letter-spacing: -0.02em; }
    .defence { border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); margin-bottom: 2.5rem; }
    .d-line { font-size: 0.98rem; line-height: 1.55; margin: 0; padding: 0.85rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); }
    .d-t { color: var(--ink-soft); margin-right: 0.9rem; font-size: 0.8rem; }
    .d-last { font-weight: 500; }
    .a-p { font-size: 1.04rem; line-height: 1.68; margin: 0 0 1.2rem; max-width: 36rem; }
    .a-strong { border-left: 2px solid var(--ink); padding-left: 1rem; }
    .a-quip { font-family: var(--font-serif); font-size: clamp(1.3rem, 1.1rem + 1.1vw, 1.8rem); line-height: 1.3; margin-block: 2rem; }
    .a-quiet { color: var(--ink-soft); }

    /* ── the reply ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
    .reply { padding-block: clamp(3rem, 2rem + 4vw, 5.5rem); border-top: 1px solid var(--rule-strong); }
    .rep-kick { font-size: 0.68rem; letter-spacing: 0.16em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink-soft); margin: 0 0 1.1rem; }
    .rep-h { font-family: var(--font-serif); font-size: clamp(1.7rem, 1.25rem + 2vw, 2.5rem); line-height: 1.15; margin: 0 0 1.75rem; }
    .rep-p { font-size: 1.04rem; line-height: 1.68; margin: 0 0 1.2rem; max-width: 36rem; }
    .rep-turn { font-family: var(--font-serif); font-size: clamp(1.35rem, 1.1rem + 1.3vw, 1.9rem); line-height: 1.3; margin-block: 2rem; max-width: 30rem; }
    .rep-quiet { color: var(--ink-soft); }

    /* ── the honest state ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
    .state { padding-block: clamp(2.5rem, 2rem + 3vw, 4rem) clamp(5rem, 4rem + 6vw, 9rem); border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); }
    .state-h { font-family: var(--font-serif); font-size: clamp(1.35rem, 1.15rem + 1vw, 1.7rem); margin: 0 0 1.25rem; }
    .state-p { font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0 0 1.1rem; max-width: 36rem; color: var(--ink-soft); }
    .state-p em { color: var(--ink); font-style: italic; }
    .src { max-width: 36rem; border-top: 2px solid var(--ink); padding-top: 1.1rem; margin: 1.75rem 0 1.25rem; display: grid; gap: 0.3rem; }
    .src-title { font-family: var(--font-serif); font-size: 1.25rem; }
    .src-meta { font-size: 0.72rem; color: var(--ink-soft); }
    .src-blurb { font-size: 0.93rem; line-height: 1.5; color: var(--ink-soft); }
    .state-more { font-size: 0.95rem; margin: 0; }

    /* ── narrow ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
    @media (max-width: 48rem) {
      /* The ledger stops being a column and becomes a footer to each step — it still empties, which
         is the only property that matters. */
      .step { grid-template-columns: 3.5rem minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 0 1rem; }
      .s-carry { grid-column: 2; margin-top: 0.7rem; padding-top: 0.6rem; border-top: 1px dashed var(--rule); }
      .s-carry li { font-size: 0.68rem; }
    }
  </style>

</BaseLayout>
